landmarks:
Use case: stylized-concept
Asset type: reusable transparent landmark sprite atlas for a modern pixel-art fantasy tactical RPG world map.
Make ONE perfectly aligned 4-column by 4-row sprite sheet, 1536x1536 canvas, TRANSPARENT BACKGROUND. All sixteen cells exactly 384x384. One isolated complete sprite per cell, centered at x=192,y=210 inside that cell with generous at least 40px clear margin on every side. No grid drawn, no text, no numbering, no labels.
Modern richly shaded pixel art. Coherent crisp square pixel clusters, 3/4 overhead miniature overworld perspective, NOT full-height side view and NOT strict diamond isometric. Warm pale limestone, cool slate shadows, weathered teal roofs, amber sunlight from upper left. Same art language across all sixteen landmarks. Detailed enough for premium modern indie RPG, but silhouette readability at 64px final display. Entire buildings and their small base/grass/sand/snow patches fit inside each cell. Transparent outer silhouette, no opaque rectangular backdrop or checkerboard.
Exactly these sixteen cells in reading order:
row 1 col 1: tiny snowy alpine village, three timber chalets with teal pitched roofs laden with white snow, two firs and warm window glows;
row 1 col 2: woodland travelers' camp, three canvas tents, a small campfire and supply crates, green ground;
row 1 col 3: fortified grain store, squat stone keep, timber granary, two wheat sacks and amber grain patch;
row 1 col 4: grim rectangular prison stockade, stone perimeter walls, complete closed corner towers, iron gate, dark courtyard;
row 2 col 1: military field camp, three ochre tents, palisade gate and rolled banners, complete footprint;
row 2 col 2: major walled harbor city, teal-roofed buildings, distinctive tall stone keep, crenellations, tiny wooden pier facing lower right with blue-water edge;
row 2 col 3: coastal stone fortress, two sturdy towers with teal pennants, gate, foundations on a gray rocky patch;
row 2 col 4: snowy mountain pass gate, thick twin stone guard towers and a clear central arched opening, snow-covered rock base;
row 3 col 1: very tall sacred sun tower, pale stone octagonal shaft, amber luminous sun lens at top, snowy circular foundation, recognizable silhouette;
row 3 col 2: royal capital, elegant large multi-tower citadel, deep teal roofs, gold banners, small surrounding rooftops, much grander than row2col2;
row 3 col 3: small graceful wooden sailing cutter, one cream triangular sail, teal pennant, dark hull, isolated ship with no sea rectangle;
row 3 col 4: large ominous prison galleon, dark wooden hull, two rust-red square sails, bars on deck, isolated ship;
row 4 col 1: oasis desert city, grouped warm sand-colored flat-roofed houses, cyan canopy, central water well and two palms;
row 4 col 2: salt-flat observatory, pale terraced stone platform, open star-lens instrument, one slim blue tower, sand-white base;
